# Overrides Tauri's built-in desktop-entry template (bundle.linux.deb.desktopTemplate).
# It exists for ONE character: the %F on Exec.
#
# Tauri 2.11.4 ships `Exec={{exec}}` with no field code, and per the freedesktop
# Desktop Entry spec an entry without one is launched with NO arguments - so a
# file manager opening a .md would start the app and the path would never reach
# argv, which is where lib.rs reads it. Double-click did nothing on Linux.
#
# Everything else is byte-for-byte Tauri's template, so keep it that way and
# re-diff it against the upstream template on a Tauri bump:
# crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/linux/freedesktop/main.desktop
# The AppImage bundler builds on the deb tree, so this one file covers both.
#
# MimeType comes from bundle.fileAssociations plus the deep-link schemes; the
# variable is available even though the config schema's docstring omits it.
# Spec: ops/docs/plans/markdown-folder.md (section 11)
[Desktop Entry]
Categories={{categories}}
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}} %F
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Icon={{icon}}
Name={{name}}
Terminal=false
Type=Application
{{#if mime_type}}
MimeType={{mime_type}}
{{/if}}
